 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Two times, two stories",
   "texto": [
    "The perfect (**cheguei**, I arrived) has a finished past action; the imperfect (**chovia**, rain) may have a background situation, a habit or an ongoing action.",
    "Example: **Quando cheguei, chovia** (when I arrived, rain). The arrival takes place during a situation that was already under way."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Enquanto y quando",
   "texto": [
    "**Enquanto** (while) usually links simultaneous actions: **Enquanto eu lia, ela dormia** (while I read, she slept).",
    "**Quando** means «when»; it does not by itself decide the verbal time. The context and meaning determine the time: **Quando chegaste, eu comia** (when you arrived, I was eating), **Quando chegaste, comecei a cozinhar** (when you arrived, I started cooking)."
   ]
  },
